  "notes": [
    "FoC debug build, Coruscant quick load, seed 12345, tick 0 at frame 345, 30 logical ticks/s; fog revealed to both players and player AI suspended.",
    "Ticks 5 to 8 script 4000 damage onto each turbolaser hardpoint (BL, BR, ML, MR). Scripted damage takes the MC80's 2000 shields first (S-18, S-19), so the first hit also has to break the shield. The hull should stay intact (HD-02). If a turbolaser survives, the recording is unusable for isolating the ion drain.",
    "The Tartan holds fire so that only the MC80 changes its shield. The attack order is GameObject.Attack_Target on tick 30.",
    "What the remake predicts, not yet observed: the forward ion cannons do the hardpoint's own 40 (DG-25) at the corvette shield multiplier. They empty the Tartan's 800 shields and then drain its energy pool with the overflow (EN-07). They never damage its hull (DP-06), so the Tartan stays alive.",
    "Record-only until the retail recording exists (#561); the remake comparison needs the MC80 of #537."
  ]
